    QuoteModel(
      id: 'csv_1230',
      authorEn: 'Epictetus', authorPt: 'Epictetus', authorEs: 'Epictetus',
      textEn: 'How long are you going to wait before you demand the best for yourself and in no instance bypass the discriminations of reason? You have been given the principles that you ought to endorse, and you have endorsed them. What kind of teacher, then, are you still waiting for in order to refer your self-improvement to him? You are no longer a boy, but a full-grown man. If you are careless and lazy now and keep putting things off and always deferring the day after which you will attend to yourself, you will not notice that you are making no progress, but you will live and die as someone quite ordinary. From now on, then, resolve to live as a grown-up who is making progress, and make whatever you think best a law that you never set aside. And whenever you encounter anything that is difficult or pleasurable, or highly or lowly regarded, remember that the contest is now: you are at the Olympic Games, you cannot wait any longer, and that your progress is wrecked or preserved by a single day and a single event. That is how Socrates fulfilled himself by attending to nothing except reason in everything he encountered. And you, although you are not yet a Socrates, should live as someone who at least wants to be a Socrates.',
      textPt: 'At\u00e9 quando vai esperar antes de exigir o melhor de si mesmo? Voc\u00ea recebeu os princ\u00edpios que deveria endossar, e os endossou. Que tipo de professor voc\u00ea ainda est\u00e1 esperando? Voc\u00ea n\u00e3o \u00e9 mais um menino, mas um homem adulto. Se for descuidado e pregui\u00e7oso agora, viver\u00e1 e morrer\u00e1 como algu\u00e9m comum. A partir de agora, resolva viver como um adulto que progride. Foi assim que S\u00f3crates se realizou. E voc\u00ea, embora n\u00e3o seja um S\u00f3crates, deveria viver como algu\u00e9m que ao menos quer ser um S\u00f3crates.',
      textEs: '\u00bfHasta cu\u00e1ndo vas a esperar antes de exigir lo mejor de ti mismo? Has recibido los principios que deb\u00edas respaldar, y los has respaldado. \u00bfQu\u00e9 tipo de maestro sigues esperando? Ya no eres un ni\u00f1o, sino un hombre adulto. Si eres descuidado y perezoso ahora, vivir\u00e1s y morir\u00e1s como alguien com\u00fan. Desde ahora, resuelve vivir como un adulto que progresa. As\u00ed fue como S\u00f3crates se realiz\u00f3. Y t\u00fa, aunque no seas un S\u00f3crates, deber\u00edas vivir como alguien que al menos quiere ser un S\u00f3crates.',
      reflectionEn: 'Stop waiting to become your best self. Begin today, in small acts and choices.',
      reflectionPt: 'Pare de esperar para se tornar sua melhor vers\u00e3o. Comece hoje, em pequenos atos e escolhas.',
      reflectionEs: 'Deja de esperar para convertirte en tu mejor versi\u00f3n. Comienza hoy, en peque\u00f1os actos y elecciones.',
      category: 'stoicism',
      moods: ['unmotivated', 'anxious', 'tired'],
    ),
